GloomhavenVR @VERSION@ — how to install it
==========================================

Auf Deutsch: INSTALL-DEUTSCH.txt (liegt neben dieser Datei)

Play Gloomhaven (digital) as a room-scale VR board game: you stand at the
table and pick your cards up with your hands.

The same guide WITH PICTURES, plus the controls and every setting:
  https://github.com/McFredward/GloomhavenVR


YOU NEED
  * Gloomhaven (digital) for PC, v1.1.x — Steam or GOG.
  * Windows and a PC-VR headset. Developed and tested on a Quest 3 over
    Virtual Desktop; Quest Link, Steam Link and SteamVR should work but are
    not tested.
  * BepInEx 5.4.23.5 — a small, free program that lets mods run at all.
    Step 1, once.

Everything else is already inside this zip.


1. INSTALL BepInEx, ONCE
   Download BepInEx_win_x64_5.4.23.5.zip from
     https://github.com/BepInEx/BepInEx/releases/tag/v5.4.23.5
   and unpack it into your Gloomhaven folder — the one with GH.exe in it.
   (On Steam: right-click the game -> Manage -> Browse local files.)

   Start the game once the normal way and quit again. A new folder BepInEx
   should now hold a file LogOutput.log. That file is your proof it worked.

2. INSTALL GloomhavenVR
   Unpack THIS zip into that same Gloomhaven folder and let Windows merge
   the BepInEx folder. Then check these two folders exist:

     BepInEx\plugins\GloomhavenVR\
     BepInEx\patchers\GloomhavenVR\

   If either is missing, unpack the zip again rather than moving files by
   hand.

3. POINT YOUR HEADSET AT THE GAME
   One setting decides which app shows PC VR games — the OpenXR runtime.
     Virtual Desktop  -> choose VDXR in the Virtual Desktop streamer settings
     Quest Link       -> Meta Quest Link app, Settings, General, OpenXR
                         Runtime, "Set Meta Quest Link as active"
     Steam Link       -> SteamVR Settings, OpenXR, "Set SteamVR as OpenXR
                         runtime"

4. START THE GAME
   Put the headset on and start Gloomhaven the way you normally do.

   THE FIRST TIME AFTER INSTALLING OR UPDATING, THE GAME CLOSES AND REOPENS
   BY ITSELF — ONCE. That is meant to happen. It is not a crash.

   Your save games and your settings are not touched.

   The mod writes exactly ONE game file: GH_Data\boot.config. The original
   is kept next to it as boot.config.gloomhavenvr-backup. If the game ever
   refuses to start, copy that backup back over boot.config.

   Why it restarts, and how to avoid it, is on the project page linked at
   the top of this file.


SETTINGS
  Everything is adjustable from inside the headset: open the game's own
  Options window and pick the VR Options tab.

  To play the game completely unmodified for a while, set Enabled = false
  under [General] in BepInEx\config\dev.gloomhavenvr.cfg. Nothing to
  uninstall.


PLAYING WITH OTHER PEOPLE
  Everyone playing together needs the same version of the mod — if two
  people differ, the game says so instead of letting the session go quietly
  wrong. People without the mod can still play with you normally.


IF SOMETHING GOES WRONG
  Game starts on your monitor, or the headset stays black? Check step 3.
  If that is right, add -force-d3d11 to the game's launch options.

  Anything else: send the whole of
    BepInEx\LogOutput.log
  say what you were doing, and say which headset you use and how you
  connect it.
